    "summaries": [
      {
        "action_date": "2025-01-09",
        "action_desc": "Introduced in House",
        "text": "<p><strong>Organ Donation Referral Improvement Act</strong></p><p>This bill requires the&nbsp;Office of the Assistant Secretary for Planning and Evaluation (ASPE) in the&nbsp;Department of Health and Human Services to conduct a study on hospitals\u2019 use of electronic automated referrals for organ donations. The bill defines <em>electronic automated referral</em> as an electronic system that uses electronic health records to identify patients who are potential organ donors and automatically refers those patients to organ procurement organizations.&nbsp;</p><p>The ASPE must include specified components in the study, including identifying benefits, reviewing best practices, and developing recommendations for the use of electronic automated referrals for organ donations. </p>",
        "update_date": "2025-03-13T19:06:30Z"
      }
    ]
  },
